  "query_preview": "below. What we will need to continue to watch is the\nstrength of the cap around 750mb, as that will prevent\ndevelopment through much of the afternoon. As surface temps hit\nthe low 80s, at the time where shear values are increasing,\nisolated cells could develop. These storms would pose the\nlargest tornado threat, along with large hail. Storm mode will\ntransition to more linear into the early evening, with the\nprimary threat becoming damaging winds. This line will push\neastward through the evening hours, with scattered showers\nhanging around portions of the Arrowhead and northwest WI for a\nfew hours past midnight.",
